# Local secrets. NEVER commit — see .env.example and docs/RUNNING.md.
.env
.env.local

# The deployed secrets, and any backup of them. This file lives on the VM next
# to docker-compose.prod.yml and holds every production credential the API has.
#
# It is UNTRACKED BY DESIGN — the deploy job runs `git reset --hard origin/main`
# in that directory and untracked files are what survive it. But untracked is
# not the same as ignored: without a rule here the file sits in `git status` as
# a staging candidate in a clone of a PUBLIC repository, one `git add -A` away
# from being published. Ignoring it also means a future `git clean -fd` skips it
# rather than deleting every production credential on the box.
.env.prod
.env.prod.*

# Firebase service account for local push testing — never commit a key.
secrets/
